<title>POLAND: Polish net reserves rise to $21.82 bln on June 10.</title>
<headline>Polish net reserves rise to $21.82 bln on June 10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency reserves grew by $105.3 million in the June 1-10 period to $21.82 billion and were $151.5 million higher than at the start of the year, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)  JUNE 1-10   MAY 97    JUNE 96</p>
<p>    Official reserves		 N.A	   N.A	17.64</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.82	 21.71     21.54</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
